dible implementation patch or produce a report\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:927:- `recovery`: preserve the round-2 artifact, terminate the lane, and relaunch an even tighter round-3 implementer prompt that names the minimum acceptable Story 4 write surface and requires immediate movement into edits plus the full gate\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:929:## Story 4 Implementation Round 3\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:939:  - client page tests now prove Story 4 visibility and empty-state rendering requirements\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:951:## Story 4 Verification Summary\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:965:- `next action`: route Story 4 fix round 1 through the CLI worker lane\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:1126:## 2026-04-15 - Story 4 local repair round 2\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:1128:- Context: the fresh post-fix primary review still returned `REVISE` because Story 4’s reader/bootstrap path had been corrected, but the durable layer still had no non-test writer surfaces for `currentArtifactIds`, `currentSourceAttachmentIds`, or current process outputs.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:1129:- Decision: took Story 4 locally instead of dispatching another async worker so the fix could be carried through implementation, verification, and artifact updates without another orchestration stall.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:1136:- Why this closes the blocker: Story 4 now has shipped durable writer paths for current material refs and current outputs, plus direct Convex-layer proof for exact-set write/read, stale clearing, linked-artifact preservation, output replacement, and cross-project validation. The app is no