ater process work and provenance read them from durable source state |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:152:| A8 | Detaching a source attachment removes it from current active use but does not erase prior process history or prior durable code-update visibility | Validated | Product + Platform | Current work and prior provenance remain distinct concerns |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:179:provenance.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:207:  is the normalized GitHub identity used for uniqueness and provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:402:In Epic 6, source provenance is durable, process-specific, and complements the\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:403:artifact-version provenance aligned in Epic 5. Epic 6 requires durable\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:404:process-specific provenance records; the exact schema is deferred to Tech\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:409:Epic 6 records provenance durably at two moments:\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:411:- `informed_work` provenance is recorded when process work uses attached sources\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:413:- `received_code_update` provenance is recorded when a durable code update lands\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:416:Provenance remains durable after detach because each provenance entry copies\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:422:Each provenance relationship resolves independently. If one provenance lookup\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:423:cannot fully enrich current attachment context, the provenance endpoint still\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:426:that provenance record.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:433:- **TC-4.1a: Informing source provenance visible**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:435:  - When: User views current source provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:437:- **TC-4.1b: Empty provenance state shown for process with no recorded source use**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:438:  - Given: A process has no recorded source provenance yet\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:439:  - When: User views current source provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:440:  - Then: The platform shows a clear empty provenance state\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:445:- **TC-4.2a: Receiving source provenance visible**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:447:  - When: User views current source provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:455:  - When: User views source provenance after code work\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:458:**AC-4.4:** One failing provenance lookup does not fail the rest of the\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:459:provenance surface.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:461:- **TC-4.4a: One degraded provenance entry does not hide healthy entries**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:462:  - Given: A process has multiple provenance relationships and one cannot fully\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:464:  - When: User loads process source provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:465:  - Then: The healthy provenance entries remain visible and the failing one is\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:467:- **TC-4.4b: Degraded provenance entry falls back to durable identity**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:468:  - Given: One provenance lookup cannot enrich current attachment metadata\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:469:  - When: The provenance surface loads\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:486:identity needed for provenance.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:491:4. System preserves prior visible provenance and prior process history\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:513:provenance or prior process history that already referenced that source.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:515:- **TC-5.2a: Prior provenance remains after detach**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:518:  - Then: Prior visible provenance and prior process history remain available\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:588:| `/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Process work surface showing current sources for that process, including process-scoped sources and applicable project-scoped sources after shadowing/conflict rules, plus source provenance |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:604:| Get process source provenance | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/source-provenance` | Returns process-specific provenance entries for attached sources that informed or received work, complementing artifact-version provenance from Epic 5; one degraded provenance lookup does not fail the whole read |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:612:| repositoryFullName | string | no | `owner/name` format when present | Normalized canonical GitHub identity used for uniqueness and provenance; may be provided by the client or derived from `repositoryUrl` during validation |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:641:| repositoryFullName | string | yes | `owner/name` format, non-empty | Normalized canonical GitHub identity used for uniqueness, conflict handling, and provenance; new in Epic 6 |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:662:| provenanceId | string | yes | non-empty | Stable provenance identifier |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:663:| sourceAttachmentId | string | no | non-empty when present | Attached source this provenance entry refers to, when the source attachment is still available |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:664:| relationshipKind | enum | yes | `informed_work` or `received_code_update` | How this source relates to the process work |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:666:| repositoryUrl | string | yes | full GitHub URL, non-empty | Operational source URL copied at the time provenance is recorded |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:668:| entryStatus | enum | yes | `ready` or `degraded` | Whether this provenance entry resolved cleanly or is returned with bounded degradation |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:669:| degradationReason | string | no | non-empty when present | Why this provenance entry is degraded when `entryStatus` is `degraded` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:670:| recordedAt | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Time this provenance relationship was recorded |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:672:These entries complement the artifact version provenance defined in Epic 5.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:707:| entries | array of Source Provenance Entry | yes | present | Process-specific provenance entries for attached sources that informed or received work |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:711:A successful provenance read may contain both `ready` and `degraded` entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:712:Per-entry provenance degradation does not force a request-level error when the\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:713:rest of the provenance surface is still readable.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:751:  references, and review/package provenance rules\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:791:- Detaching a source does not erase prior visible provenance or prior process\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:795:- One degraded provenance lookup does not fail the rest of the provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:824:   source attachments, including canonical repository identity and provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:834:5. What exact provenance surface should show informed-work relationships and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:836:   artifact-version provenance from Epic 5?\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:844:   provenance visibility while excluding detached attachments from current\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:852:this epic owns artifact-model migration or review/package provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:858:repository identity contracts, provenance shapes, error classes, hydration and\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:859:freshness fixtures for the four-state model, Epic 5-aligned material/provenance\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:897:### Story 4: Provenance and Canonical Source Visibility\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:900:received process work, and the provenance surface degrades one failing lookup\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:905:- AC-4.1 (informing source provenance visible)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:906:- AC-4.2 (receiving source provenance visible)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:908:- AC-4.4 (one failing provenance lookup degrades independently)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:914:**Prerequisite:** Story 4\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:918:- AC-5.2 (prior provenance remains after detach)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:17:| AC-2.2 | TC-2.2a, TC-2.2b | Story 2 | `convex/artifacts.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | Version provenance remains visible across histories |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:23:| AC-4.1 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.1b | Story 4 | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/package-review-panel.test.ts` | Mixed-producer package publication within one project |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:24:| AC-4.2 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.2b, TC-4.2c | Story 4 | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts`; `convex/processPackageContexts.test.ts` | Current package-building context rule |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:25:| AC-4.3 | TC-4.3a, TC-4.3b | Story 4 | `tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts` | Package member pin stability |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:26:| AC-4.4 | TC-4.4a, TC-4.4b | Story 4 | `tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/package-review-panel.test.ts` | Mixed-producer package review and export |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:38:| Path 1.3 | Persist a later-process revision as a new version with visible provenance and updated latest-version summary | Story 2 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.2a, TC-2.3a | `convex/artifacts.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:41:| Path 2.1 | Seed a current package-building context from current refs and earlier pinned versions | Story 4 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.2c | `convex/processPackageContexts.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:42:| Path 2.2 | Publish one mixed-producer package from valid same-project current context | Story 4 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.2b | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:43:| Path 2.3 | Reopen the package later and keep pinned member versions stable even when newer artifact versions now exist | Story 4 | TC-4.3a, TC-4.3b | `tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-2.md:1:# Story 4 Fix Round 2\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-2.md:21:The Story 4 blocker is closed: current materials and outputs now have shipped durable writer paths plus direct Convex-layer verification, rather than depending only on seeded `InMemoryPlatformStore` state in service tests.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’m starting by reading the required Story 4 artifacts in the order you gave, beginning with the Convex guidelines so the implementation stays aligned with project rules.\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:6:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ve loaded the Convex rules and I’m moving through the Story 4 artifacts now so I can isolate the two verified blockers without drifting into Story 5 or 6.\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:8:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Story 4: Materials and Outputs\\n\\n### Summary\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\nKeep the current artifacts, outputs, and source attachments visible so the user can follow what the process is working with right now.\\n\\n### Description\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n**User Profile**\\n\\n- **Primary User:** A technical founder, tech lead, staff engineer, or agentic operator who wants to run high-quality crafted processes through one durable project surface instead of manually stitching together prompts, tools, documents, and environments.\\n- **Context:** The user has opened a concrete process inside a project and needs to do the work of that process, not just manage shell-level summaries.\\n- **Mental Model:** \\\"I am inside one process. The process has a current phase, a running work history, current materials, and clear points where I need to respond, review, or let it continue.\\\"\\n- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\n\\n**Objective**\\n\\nShow the current materials and outputs relevant to the active phase, keep identity and revision context clear, and define how materials-state replacements update the visible workspace when current process focus changes.\\n\\n**Scope**\\n\\nIn:\\n\\n- Show current artifacts, current outputs, and current source attachments alongside process work\\n- Make current identity and revision context visible for artifacts and outputs\\n- Replace visible materials state when phase, output revision, or focus changes\\n- Show a deliberate empty state when no current materials apply\\n\\nOut:\\n\\n- Detailed review rendering for materials and outputs\\n- Side-work summaries and attention-required state treatment\\n- WebSocket subscription lifecycle, reconnect, and degraded loading behavior\\n\\n**Dependencies**\\n\\n- Story 3 conversation/current-request slice\\n- Shared live-update vocabulary from Story 0 for fixture-applied `materials` snapshots and upserts\\n- Shared bootstrap/materials vocabulary from Story 0\\n- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md), [tech-design-client.md](../tech-design-client.md), [tech-design-server.md](../tech-design-server.md)\\n- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n**AC-4.1:** The work surface keeps current phase-relevant artifacts, versions, source attachments, and current outputs visible alongside active process work.\\n\\n- **TC-4.1a: Materials visible alongside process history**\\n  - Given: Process has current materials and outputs relevant to the active phase\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\n  - Then: The materials remain visible alongside the active process work rather than being hidden behind a separate later-only surface\\n- **TC-4.1b: Source attachments visible when relevant**\\n  - Given: Process is working from one or more attached sources\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\n  - Then: The relevant source attachments are visible with the process work\\n\\n**AC-4.2:** The visible materials make the current identity and revision context clear enough that the user can tell which artifact, version, source, or output the process is currently using or revising.\\n\\n- **TC-4.2a: Current revision context visible for artifact**\\n  - Given: Process is using or revising an artifact with a current revision\\n  - When: The artifact appears in the work surface\\n  - Then: Its current identity and revision context are visible\\n- **TC-4.2b: Current output identity visible**\\n  - Given: Process has a current output in progress\\n  - When: The output appears in the work surface\\n  - Then: The user can tell which output the process is currently working on\\n\\n**AC-4.3:** When the process changes phase, revises an output, or switches focus, the visible materials update to match the current working context without requiring the user to infer the change from history alone.\\n\\n- **TC-4.3a: Phase change updates visible materials**\\n  - Given: User is viewing a process work surface\\n  - When: The process advances into a new phase with different current materials\\n  - Then: The visible materials update to the new current set\\n- **TC-4.3b: Output revision updates visible context**\\n  - Given: Process revises an output while the user is viewing the work surface\\n  - When: The revision becomes current\\n  - Then: The visible output context updates to the new current revision\\n\\n**AC-4.4:** If no current materials or outputs are relevant to the active phase, the work surface shows a clear empty state instead of stale or carried-forward context.\\n\\n- **TC-4.4a: Empty materials state shown for phase with no current materials**\\n  - Given: Active process phase has no current materials or outputs to show\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\n  - Then: The materials area shows a clear empty state\\n- **TC-4.4b: Previous materials do not linger as current**\\n  - Given: Prior phase had visible materials but the current phase does not\\n  - When: The user enters the new phase\\n  - Then: The work surface does not keep showing the old materials as if they are still current\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\nThis story uses the shared materials envelope and its artifact, output, and source reference shapes to present the current working context. It also defines the materials-specific replacement semantics used when the current working context changes. The shared WebSocket subscription lifecycle remains owned by Story 6.\\n\\n#### Process Materials Section Envelope\\n\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `status` | enum | yes | `ready`, `empty`, or `error` | Whether the materials section loaded with visible content, loaded empty, or failed independently |\\n| `currentArtifacts` | array of Process Artifact Reference | yes | present | Current artifacts relevant to the active process; empty when `status` is `empty` or `error` |\\n| `currentOutputs` | array of Process Output Reference | yes | present | Current process-owned outputs relevant to the active process, including outputs that may not yet be published as durable artifacts; empty when `status` is `empty` or `error` |\\n| `currentSources` | array of Process Source Reference | yes | present | Current source attachments relevant to the active process; empty when `status` is `empty` or `error` |\\n| `error` | Process Surface Section Error | no | present when `status` is `error` | Section-scoped load error shown without failing the whole process surface |\\n\\nThe materials envelope is the full current-state payload for the materials panel. When materials change, the client replaces the current panel state with the new envelope rather than patching individual rows in place.\\n\\n#### Process Artifact Reference\\n\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `artifactId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable artifact identifier |\\n| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Artifact display name |\\n| `currentVersionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Current revision or version label |\\n| `roleLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Why this artifact is currently relevant to the process |\\n| `updatedAt` | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Most recent durable artifact update time |\\n\\n**Sort order:** Current artifacts are ordered by `updatedAt` descending.\\n\\n#### Process Output Reference\\n\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `outputId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable output identifier |\\n| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Current output display name |\\n| `revisionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Current output revision label |\\n| `state` | string | yes | non-empty | User-visible current output state |\\n| `updatedAt` | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Most recent output update time |\\n\\n**Sort order:** Current outputs are ordered by `updatedAt` descending.\\n\\nWhen a current output already corresponds to a current artifact or current artifact version shown in `currentArtifacts`, the work surface links to that artifact context and does not show a second unconnected duplicate entry in `currentOutputs`. `currentOutputs` is reserved for outputs still in progress, outputs not yet published as durable artifacts, or outputs that still need separate current-state visibility.\\n\\n#### Process Source Reference\\n\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `sourceAttachmentId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable source attachment identifier |\\n| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Source display name |\\n| `purpose` | enum | yes | `research`, `review`, `implementation`, or `other` | Why the source is attached |\\n| `targetRef` | string | no | non-empty when present | Branch, tag, or commit ref if known |\\n| `hydrationState` | enum | yes | `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, or `unavailable` | High-level source availability state |\\n| `updatedAt` | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Most recent durable source update time |\\n\\n**Sort order:** Current sources are ordered by `updatedAt` descending.\\n\\n#### Materials Update Semantics\\n\\n| Message Shape | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `entityType: materials`, `messageType: snapshot` | Replace the current materials panel with the provided `ProcessMaterialsSectionEnvelope` snapshot |\\n| `entityType: materials`, `messageType: upsert` | Replace the current materials panel with the new current materials envelope after a phase, output, or focus change |\\n\\n#### Story-Specific Notes\\n\\n- TC-4.3a, TC-4.3b, and TC-4.4b are materials-slice behaviors exercised through fixture-applied `materials` snapshots/upserts in client store tests and published materials updates in server live-update tests.\\n- Story 4 owns the meaning of a changed `materials` payload.\\n- Story 6 owns the transport lifecycle that delivers those materials updates over the live subscription.\\n\\nSee the tech design document for full architecture, implementation targets, and test mapping.\\n\\n### Definition of Done\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n- Materials render alongside active process work rather than behind a separate review-only surface\\n- Current artifact, output, and source identity/revision context is legible in the workspace\\n- Phase changes and output revision changes replace the visible materials state without forcing inference from history\\n- Empty-materials states clear stale prior context\\n- Materials snapshot/upsert replacement semantics are defined for this slice even though the shared subscription lifecycle lands in Story 6\\n- Story tests cover TC-4.1a through TC-4.4b\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/fix-list-round-1.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Fix List Round 1: Story 4 Materials and Outputs\\n\\n## Blocking Findings\\n\\n### 1. Durable bootstrap does not derive truly current materials\\n\\n- Severity: `HIGH`\\n- Evidence:\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:22)\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:64)\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:89)\\n- Problem:\\n  - the reader filters by `processId` only and does not derive “current phase-relevant” materials from phase/focus-specific refs\\n  - stale prior process materials can reappear after reload/return-later\\n  - relevant project-scoped shared materials cannot appear as current process materials\\n- Required fix:\\n  - derive current materials from the actual current process focus rules available in this codebase\\n  - prove stale prior materials do not return on bootstrap after a phase/context change\\n  - prove relevant shared/project-scoped materials can surface when they are the current process materials\\n\\n### 2. Output/artifact dedupe uses heuristic labels instead of real linkage\\n\\n- Severity: `MEDIUM`\\n- Evidence:\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:15)\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:37)\\n  - [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:6)\\n  - [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:27)\\n- Problem:\\n  - `linkedArtifactId` exists in durable outputs, but the reader dedupes via display name plus revision\\n  - unrelated outputs can be hidden if labels collide\\n  - linked pairs can still duplicate if labels drift\\n- Required fix:\\n  - carry the actual artifact linkage through the reader path or otherwise dedupe on real identity, not display heuristics\\n  - add server/API coverage proving dedupe on real linkage\\n\\n## Verification Expectations For Fix Round\\n\\n- rerun:\\n  - `corepack pnpm run red-verify && corepack pnpm run test:service && corepack pnpm run test:client`\\n- add or update server/API tests, not only client fixture/reducer tests\\n- stay inside Story 4 scope; do not pull Story 6 transport lifecycle into the fix\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-review.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"1. Verdict: REVISE\\n\\n2. Findings:\\n- High: Durable bootstrap still does not model “current materials”; it just returns every process-scoped artifact/source row. [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:22), [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:64), [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:89). The reader filters by `processId` only and never consults phase/focus-specific refs, so prior process materials can reappear after reload/return-later, and relevant project-scoped shared materials cannot appear at all. That misses Story 4’s “current phase-relevant” requirement and weakens the stale-context clearing behavior in AC-4.3/4.4.\\n- Medium: Output/artifact deduplication is using a display-name-plus-revision heuristic instead of the actual artifact link. [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:15), [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:37), [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:6), [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:27). The durable table has `linkedArtifactId`, but that linkage is dropped before the reader runs, so unrelated outputs can be hidden if they share name/revision with an artifact, and true linked pairs can still duplicate if labels drift. That makes Story 4’s output identity/no-dup semantics unreliable.\\n\\n3. Gate result with exact command and pass/fail:\\n- `corepack pnpm run red-verify && corepack pnpm run test:service && corepack pnpm run test:client` -> PASS\\n\\n4. Residual risks or test gaps:\\n- Server-side coverage does not prove bootstrap clears stale materials across a phase change/reload path; current Story 4 coverage is mostly client page/reducer fixture coverage.\\n- There is no service/API test for project-scoped shared materials being surfaced as current process materials, or for dedupe based on a real artifact link rather than the current name/revision heuristic.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-impl-round-3.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Codex Implementer Report: Story 4 Materials and Outputs\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n- [process-materials-section.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts)\\n- [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts)\\n- [live-process.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/fixtures/live-process.ts)\\n- [materials.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/fixtures/materials.ts)\\n- [process-live.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts)\\n- [process-work-surface-page.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts)\\n\\n## Claimed Behavior\\n\\n- Current artifacts, outputs, and source attachments remain visible beside active process work in the work surface.\\n- Each material now renders clearer identity and context:\\n  - artifacts show `Artifact ID`, current version, optional role, and updated timestamp\\n  - outputs show `Output ID`, current revision, state, and updated timestamp\\n  - sources show `Source ID`, purpose, hydration state, optional target ref, and updated timestamp\\n- Materials `snapshot` and `upsert` handling continue to replace the whole materials envelope; Story 4 tests now prove phase-change and output-revision updates replace the visible materials state instead of carrying stale rows forward.\\n- Empty materials envelopes render a deliberate empty state, and empty snapshots clear stale prior artifact/output/source context.\\n\\n## Gate Result\\n\\n- `corepack pnpm run red-verify`\\n  - first pass failed on formatter output only\\n  - after applying formatter, rerun passed\\n- `corepack pnpm run test:service` -> `PASS` (`8` files / `52` tests)\\n- `corepack pnpm run test:client` -> `PASS` (`14` files / `87` tests)\\n\\n## Claimed Residual Risks\\n\\n- Server materials behavior was intentionally kept minimal in this round; coverage is concentrated on client rendering plus live materials-envelope replacement semantics.\\n- No Story 5 side-work treatment or Story 6 transport lifecycle/reconnect behavior was introduced.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ve confirmed the current reader is only doing process-wide filtering. Next I’m finding the actual “current material” fields already available in durable data so we can derive the Story 4 panel from real focus state instead of broad process membership.\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:51:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_26\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"phase change|context change|shared/project-scoped|published_to_artifact|output revision|dedupe\\\\\\\" docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface -g '\\\"'!**/node_modules/**'\\\"'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-client.md:405:| TC-4.3a | phase change updates materials | `tests/service/client/process-live-store.test.ts` | Live materials upsert | Materials view updates |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-client.md:406:| TC-4.3b | output revision updates visible context | `tests/service/client/process-live-store.test.ts` | Output upsert | Revision context updates |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-client.md:460:| TC-2.2b | phase change visible while open | `tests/service/client/process-live-store.test.ts` | Phase upsert | Phase label updates |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/test-plan.md:341:| TC-4.3b | `TC-4.3b output revision upsert updates current output context` | Existing output state | Apply materials upsert | Output revision updated |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:582:| TC-4.3a | phase change updates materials | `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts` | Process module changes material refs | Live materials update published |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:583:| TC-4.3b | output revision updates visible context | `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts` | Output row patched | Live materials update published |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/tech-design-server.md:673:| TC-2.2b | phase change visible while open | `tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts` | Phase update published | Phase message emitted |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/epic.md:685:| revisionLabel | string | no | non-empty when present | Current output revision label |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md:26:- Replace visible materials state when phase, output revision, or focus changes\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md:91:This story uses the shared materials envelope and its artifact, output, and source reference shapes to present the current working context. It also defines the materials-specific replacement semantics used when the current working context changes. The shared WebSocket subscription lifecycle remains owned by Story 6.\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md:123:| `revisionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Current output revision label |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md:163:- Phase changes and output revision changes replace the visible materials state without forcing inference from history\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/02-start-and-resume.md:114:| `process.phaseLabel` | Reflect visible phase changes while the process remains open |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/05-side-work-visibility.md:32:- Deep materials review and output revision behavior\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/06-live-reconciliation-and-degradation.md:27:- Show live status and phase changes while active work is happening\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/06-live-reconciliation-and-degradation.md:204:- Live status and phase changes appear without requiring manual refresh\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap.md:197:| `revisionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Current output revision label |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:938:  - client live materials tests now prove envelope replacement on phase change, output revision, and empty-state clearing\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:963:  - output/artifact dedupe still relies on display-name-plus-revision heuristics instead of the real artifact linkage\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:8:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# Story 4: Materials and Outputs\\\\n\\\\n### Summary\\\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\\\nKeep the current artifacts, outputs, and source attachments visible so the user can follow what the process is working with right now.\\\\n\\\\n### Description\\\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\\\n**User Profile**\\\\n\\\\n- **Primary User:** A technical founder, tech lead, staff engineer, or agentic operator who wants to run high-quality crafted processes through one durable project surface instead of manually stitching together prompts, tools, documents, and environments.\\\\n- **Context:** The user has opened a concrete process inside a project and needs to do the work of that process, not just manage shell-level summaries.\\\\n- **Mental Model:** \\\\\\\"I am inside one process. The process has a current phase, a running work history, current materials, and clear points where I need to respond, review, or let it continue.\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\\\n\\\\n**Objective**\\\\n\\\\nShow the current materials and outputs relevant to the active phase, keep identity and revision context clear, and define how materials-state replacements update the visible workspace when current process focus changes.\\\\n\\\\n**Scope**\\\\n\\\\nIn:\\\\n\\\\n- Show current artifacts, current outputs, and current source attachments alongside process work\\\\n- Make current identity and revision context visible for artifacts and outputs\\\\n- Replace visible materials state when phase, output revision, or focus changes\\\\n- Show a deliberate empty state when no current materials apply\\\\n\\\\nOut:\\\\n\\\\n- Detailed review rendering for materials and outputs\\\\n- Side-work summaries and attention-required state treatment\\\\n- WebSocket subscription lifecycle, reconnect, and degraded loading behavior\\\\n\\\\n**Dependencies**\\\\n\\\\n- Story 3 conversation/current-request slice\\\\n- Shared live-update vocabulary from Story 0 for fixture-applied `materials` snapshots and upserts\\\\n- Shared bootstrap/materials vocabulary from Story 0\\\\n- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md), [tech-design-client.md](../tech-design-client.md), [tech-design-server.md](../tech-design-server.md)\\\\n- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\\\\n\\\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\\\n**AC-4.1:** The work surface keeps current phase-relevant artifacts, versions, source attachments, and current outputs visible alongside active process work.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.1a: Materials visible alongside process history**\\\\n  - Given: Process has current materials and outputs relevant to the active phase\\\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\\\n  - Then: The materials remain visible alongside the active process work rather than being hidden behind a separate later-only surface\\\\n- **TC-4.1b: Source attachments visible when relevant**\\\\n  - Given: Process is working from one or more attached sources\\\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\\\n  - Then: The relevant source attachments are visible with the process work\\\\n\\\\n**AC-4.2:** The visible materials make the current identity and revision context clear enough that the user can tell which artifact, version, source, or output the process is currently using or revising.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.2a: Current revision context visible for artifact**\\\\n  - Given: Process is using or revising an artifact with a current revision\\\\n  - When: The artifact appears in the work surface\\\\n  - Then: Its current identity and revision context are visible\\\\n- **TC-4.2b: Current output identity visible**\\\\n  - Given: Process has a current output in progress\\\\n  - When: The output appears in the work surface\\\\n  - Then: The user can tell which output the process is currently working on\\\\n\\\\n**AC-4.3:** When the process changes phase, revises an output, or switches focus, the visible materials update to match the current working context without requiring the user to infer the change from history alone.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.3a: Phase change updates visible materials**\\\\n  - Given: User is viewing a process work surface\\\\n  - When: The process advances into a new phase with different current materials\\\\n  - Then: The visible materials update to the new current set\\\\n- **TC-4.3b: Output revision updates visible context**\\\\n  - Given: Process revises an output while the user is viewing the work surface\\\\n  - When: The revision becomes current\\\\n  - Then: The visible output context updates to the new current revision\\\\n\\\\n**AC-4.4:** If no current materials or outputs are relevant to the active phase, the work surface shows a clear empty state instead of stale or carried-forward context.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.4a: Empty materials state shown for phase with no current materials**\\\\n  - Given: Active process phase has no current materials or outputs to show\\\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\\\n  - Then: The materials area shows a clear empty state\\\\n- **TC-4.4b: Previous materials do not linger as current**\\\\n  - Given: Prior phase had visible materials but the current phase does not\\\\n  - When: The user enters the new phase\\\\n  - Then: The work surface does not keep showing the old materials as if they are still current\\\\n\\\\n### Technical Design\\\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\\\nThis story uses the shared materials envelope and its artifact, output, and source reference shapes to present the current working context. It also defines the materials-specific replacement semantics used when the current working context changes. The shared WebSocket subscription lifecycle remains owned by Story 6.\\\\n\\\\n#### Process Materials Section Envelope\\\\n\\\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| `status` | enum | yes | `ready`, `empty`, or `error` | Whether the materials section loaded with visible content, loaded empty, or failed independently |\\\\n| `currentArtifacts` | array of Process Artifact Reference | yes | present | Current artifacts relevant to the active process; empty when `status` is `empty` or `error` |\\\\n| `currentOutputs` | array of Process Output Reference | yes | present | Current process-owned outputs relevant to the active process, including outputs that may not yet be published as durable artifacts; empty when `status` is `empty` or `error` |\\\\n| `currentSources` | array of Process Source Reference | yes | present | Current source attachments relevant to the active process; empty when `status` is `empty` or `error` |\\\\n| `error` | Process Surface Section Error | no | present when `status` is `error` | Section-scoped load error shown without failing the whole process surface |\\\\n\\\\nThe materials envelope is the full current-state payload for the materials panel. When materials change, the client replaces the current panel state with the new envelope rather than patching individual rows in place.\\\\n\\\\n#### Process Artifact Reference\\\\n\\\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| `artifactId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable artifact identifier |\\\\n| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Artifact display name |\\\\n| `currentVersionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Current revision or version label |\\\\n| `roleLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Why this artifact is currently relevant to the process |\\\\n| `updatedAt` | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Most recent durable artifact update time |\\\\n\\\\n**Sort order:** Current artifacts are ordered by `updatedAt` descending.\\\\n\\\\n#### Process Output Reference\\\\n\\\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| `outputId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable output identifier |\\\\n| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Current output display name |\\\\n| `revisionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Current output revision label |\\\\n| `state` | string | yes | non-empty | User-visible current output state |\\\\n| `updatedAt` | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Most recent output update time |\\\\n\\\\n**Sort order:** Current outputs are ordered by `updatedAt` descending.\\\\n\\\\nWhen a current output already corresponds to a current artifact or current artifact version shown in `currentArtifacts`, the work surface links to that artifact context and does not show a second unconnected duplicate entry in `currentOutputs`. `currentOutputs` is reserved for outputs still in progress, outputs not yet published as durable artifacts, or outputs that still need separate current-state visibility.\\\\n\\\\n#### Process Source Reference\\\\n\\\\n| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| `sourceAttachmentId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable source attachment identifier |\\\\n| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Source display name |\\\\n| `purpose` | enum | yes | `research`, `review`, `implementation`, or `other` | Why the source is attached |\\\\n| `targetRef` | string | no | non-empty when present | Branch, tag, or commit ref if known |\\\\n| `hydrationState` | enum | yes | `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, or `unavailable` | High-level source availability state |\\\\n| `updatedAt` | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Most recent durable source update time |\\\\n\\\\n**Sort order:** Current sources are ordered by `updatedAt` descending.\\\\n\\\\n#### Materials Update Semantics\\\\n\\\\n| Message Shape | Meaning |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| `entityType: materials`, `messageType: snapshot` | Replace the current materials panel with the provided `ProcessMaterialsSectionEnvelope` snapshot |\\\\n| `entityType: materials`, `messageType: upsert` | Replace the current materials panel with the new current materials envelope after a phase, output, or focus change |\\\\n\\\\n#### Story-Specific Notes\\\\n\\\\n- TC-4.3a, TC-4.3b, and TC-4.4b are materials-slice behaviors exercised through fixture-applied `materials` snapshots/upserts in client store tests and published materials updates in server live-update tests.\\\\n- Story 4 owns the meaning of a changed `materials` payload.\\\\n- Story 6 owns the transport lifecycle that delivers those materials updates over the live subscription.\\\\n\\\\nSee the tech design document for full architecture, implementation targets, and test mapping.\\\\n\\\\n### Definition of Done\\\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\\\n- Materials render alongside active process work rather than behind a separate review-only surface\\\\n- Current artifact, output, and source identity/revision context is legible in the workspace\\\\n- Phase changes and output revision changes replace the visible materials state without forcing inference from history\\\\n- Empty-materials states clear stale prior context\\\\n- Materials snapshot/upsert replacement semantics are defined for this slice even though the shared subscription lifecycle lands in Story 6\\\\n- Story tests cover TC-4.1a through TC-4.4b\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:10:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/fix-list-round-1.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# Fix List Round 1: Story 4 Materials and Outputs\\\\n\\\\n## Blocking Findings\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Durable bootstrap does not derive truly current materials\\\\n\\\\n- Severity: `HIGH`\\\\n- Evidence:\\\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:22)\\\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:64)\\\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:89)\\\\n- Problem:\\\\n  - the reader filters by `processId` only and does not derive “current phase-relevant” materials from phase/focus-specific refs\\\\n  - stale prior process materials can reappear after reload/return-later\\\\n  - relevant project-scoped shared materials cannot appear as current process materials\\\\n- Required fix:\\\\n  - derive current materials from the actual current process focus rules available in this codebase\\\\n  - prove stale prior materials do not return on bootstrap after a phase/context change\\\\n  - prove relevant shared/project-scoped materials can surface when they are the current process materials\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Output/artifact dedupe uses heuristic labels instead of real linkage\\\\n\\\\n- Severity: `MEDIUM`\\\\n- Evidence:\\\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:15)\\\\n  - [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:37)\\\\n  - [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:6)\\\\n  - [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:27)\\\\n- Problem:\\\\n  - `linkedArtifactId` exists in durable outputs, but the reader dedupes via display name plus revision\\\\n  - unrelated outputs can be hidden if labels collide\\\\n  - linked pairs can still duplicate if labels drift\\\\n- Required fix:\\\\n  - carry the actual artifact linkage through the reader path or otherwise dedupe on real identity, not display heuristics\\\\n  - add server/API coverage proving dedupe on real linkage\\\\n\\\\n## Verification Expectations For Fix Round\\\\n\\\\n- rerun:\\\\n  - `corepack pnpm run red-verify && corepack pnpm run test:service && corepack pnpm run test:client`\\\\n- add or update server/API tests, not only client fixture/reducer tests\\\\n- stay inside Story 4 scope; do not pull Story 6 transport lifecycle into the fix\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:12:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-review.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"1. Verdict: REVISE\\\\n\\\\n2. Findings:\\\\n- High: Durable bootstrap still does not model “current materials”; it just returns every process-scoped artifact/source row. [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:22), [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:64), [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:89). The reader filters by `processId` only and never consults phase/focus-specific refs, so prior process materials can reappear after reload/return-later, and relevant project-scoped shared materials cannot appear at all. That misses Story 4’s “current phase-relevant” requirement and weakens the stale-context clearing behavior in AC-4.3/4.4.\\\\n- Medium: Output/artifact deduplication is using a display-name-plus-revision heuristic instead of the actual artifact link. [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:15), [materials-section.reader.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:37), [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:6), [processOutputs.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/processOutputs.ts:27). The durable table has `linkedArtifactId`, but that linkage is dropped before the reader runs, so unrelated outputs can be hidden if they share name/revision with an artifact, and true linked pairs can still duplicate if labels drift. That makes Story 4’s output identity/no-dup semantics unreliable.\\\\n\\\\n3. Gate result with exact command and pass/fail:\\\\n- `corepack pnpm run red-verify && corepack pnpm run test:service && corepack pnpm run test:client` -> PASS\\\\n\\\\n4. Residual risks or test gaps:\\\\n- Server-side coverage does not prove bootstrap clears stale materials across a phase change/reload path; current Story 4 coverage is mostly client page/reducer fixture coverage.\\\\n- There is no service/API test for project-scoped shared materials being surfaced as current process materials, or for dedupe based on a real artifact link rather than the current name/revision heuristic.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:17:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,240p' apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"import {\\\\n  type ArtifactSummary,\\\\n  type ProcessArtifactReference,\\\\n  type ProcessMaterialsSectionEnvelope,\\\\n  type ProcessOutputReference,\\\\n  type ProcessSourceReference,\\\\n  processMaterialsSectionEnvelopeSchema,\\\\n} from '../../../../shared/contracts/index.js';\\\\nimport type { PlatformStore } from '../../projects/platform-store.js';\\\\n\\\\nfunction sortByUpdatedAtDesc<T extends { updatedAt: string }>(items: T[]): T[] {\\\\n  return [...items].sort((left, right) => right.updatedAt.localeCompare(left.updatedAt));\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nfunction toArtifactIdentityKey(args: {\\\\n  displayName: string;\\\\n  currentVersionLabel: string | null;\\\\n}): string {\\\\n  return `${args.displayName}::${args.currentVersionLabel ?? ''}`;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nfunction buildCurrentArtifacts(args: {\\\\n  artifacts: ArtifactSummary[];\\\\n  processId: string;\\\\n}): ProcessArtifactReference[] {\\\\n  return sortByUpdatedAtDesc(\\\\n    args.artifacts.filter((artifact) => artifact.processId === args.processId),\\\\n  ).map((artifact) => ({\\\\n    artifactId: artifact.artifactId,\\\\n    displayName: artifact.displayName,\\\\n    currentVersionLabel: artifact.currentVersionLabel,\\\\n    roleLabel: artifact.attachmentScope === 'process' ? 'Current working artifact' : null,\\\\n    updatedAt: artifact.updatedAt,\\\\n  }));\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nfunction buildCurrentOutputs(args: {\\\\n  outputs: ProcessOutputReference[];\\\\n  currentArtifacts: ProcessArtifactReference[];\\\\n}): ProcessOutputReference[] {\\\\n  const currentArtifactIdentities = new Set(\\\\n    args.currentArtifacts.map((artifact) =>\\\\n      toArtifactIdentityKey({\\\\n        displayName: artifact.displayName,\\\\n        currentVersionLabel: artifact.currentVersionLabel,\\\\n      }),\\\\n    ),\\\\n  );\\\\n\\\\n  return sortByUpdatedAtDesc(args.outputs).filter((output) => {\\\\n    if (output.state !== 'published_to_artifact') {\\\\n      return true;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    return !currentArtifactIdentities.has(\\\\n      toArtifactIdentityKey({\\\\n        displayName: output.displayName,\\\\n        currentVersionLabel: output.revisionLabel,\\\\n      }),\\\\n    );\\\\n  });\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nfunction buildCurrentSources(args: {\\\\n  sourceAttachments: Awaited<ReturnType<PlatformStore['listProjectSourceAttachments']>>;\\\\n  processId: string;\\\\n}): ProcessSourceReference[] {\\\\n  return sortByUpdatedAtDesc(\\\\n    args.sourceAttachments.filter(\\\\n      (sourceAttachment) => sourceAttachment.processId === args.processId,\\\\n    ),\\\\n  ).map((sourceAttachment) => ({\\\\n    sourceAttachmentId: sourceAttachment.sourceAttachmentId,\\\\n    displayName: sourceAttachment.displayName,\\\\n    purpose: sourceAttachment.purpose,\\\\n    targetRef: sourceAttachment.targetRef,\\\\n    hydrationState: sourceAttachment.hydrationState,\\\\n    updatedAt: sourceAttachment.updatedAt,\\\\n  }));\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport class MaterialsSectionReader {\\\\n  constructor(private readonly platformStore: PlatformStore) {}\\\\n\\\\n  async read(args: {\\\\n    projectId: string;\\\\n    processId: string;\\\\n  }): Promise<ProcessMaterialsSectionEnvelope> {\\\\n    const [artifacts, outputs, sourceAttachments] = await Promise.all([\\\\n      this.platformStore.listProjectArtifacts({\\\\n        projectId: args.projectId,\\\\n      }),\\\\n      this.platformStore.listProcessOutputs({\\\\n        processId: args.processId,\\\\n      }),\\\\n      this.platformStore.listProjectSourceAttachments({\\\\n        projectId: args.projectId,\\\\n      }),\\\\n    ]);\\\\n\\\\n    const currentArtifacts = buildCurrentArtifacts({\\\\n      artifacts,\\\\n      processId: args.processId,\\\\n    });\\\\n    const currentOutputs = buildCurrentOutputs({\\\\n      outputs,\\\\n      currentArtifacts,\\\\n    });\\\\n    const currentSources = buildCurrentSources({\\\\n      sourceAttachments,\\\\n      processId: args.processId,\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    return processMaterialsSectionEnvelopeSchema.parse({\\\\n      status:\\\\n        currentArtifacts.length > 0 || currentOutputs.length > 0 || currentSources.length > 0\\\\n          ? 'ready'\\\\n          : 'empty',\\\\n      currentArtifacts,\\\\n      currentOutputs,\\\\n      currentSources,\\\\n    });\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:21:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"current materials|currentArtifacts|currentSources|currentOutputs|linkedArtifactId|focus|phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" apps/platform convex tests -g '\\\\\\\"'!**/node_modules/**'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"tests/service/client/project-router.test.ts:239:  it('TC-4.4c keeps a valid selected process focused from route state', async () => {\\\\ntests/service/client/process-router.test.ts:45:  phaseLabel: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.phaseLabel,\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:18:  phaseChangedProcessMaterialsFixture,\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:206:  it('TC-4.3a phase changes replace the visible materials envelope', () => {\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:212:    expect(nextState.materials).toEqual(phaseChangedProcessMaterialsFixture);\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:213:    expect(nextState.materials?.currentArtifacts).toEqual(\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:214:      phaseChangedProcessMaterialsFixture.currentArtifacts,\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:216:    expect(nextState.materials?.currentArtifacts).not.toEqual(\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:217:      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentArtifacts,\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:219:    expect(nextState.materials?.currentSources).not.toEqual(\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:220:      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources,\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:231:    expect(nextState.materials?.currentOutputs).toEqual(\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:232:      revisedOutputProcessMaterialsFixture.currentOutputs,\\\\ntests/service/client/process-live.test.ts:234:    expect(nextState.materials?.currentOut