ge.ts:71-99), the source attachment section is read-only markup with no form/button/callback (apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts:24-69), and the process work surface only renders existing controls/materials/history/side-work with no attach affordance or handler (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-work-surface-page.ts:183-221). No client module calls the new POST /api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments or /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments routes, so a user cannot complete TC-1.1a or TC-1.1b from the required UI surfaces.\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:704:          - \\\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts\\\"\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:716:        evidence: \\\"AC-1.2 requires the new attachment's repository identity and chosen scope to be visible immediately after creation (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29-30,60-65). The process-surface contract cannot carry that data: ProcessSourceReference omits repositoryFullName and attachmentScope (apps/platform/shared/contracts/process-work-surface.ts:318-330), the materials reader only projects displayName/purpose/accessMode/repositoryUrl/targetRef/hydrationState/updatedAt into currentSources (apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:90-99), and the process materials UI renders purpose/access/hydration/target ref/updated only (apps/platform/client/features/processes/process-materials-section.ts:220-253). The process attach API test likewise asserts only displayName and 