/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"]}],\"baselineBeforeStory\":611,\"baselineAfterStory\":613,\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\"]},\"cumulativeBaseline\":{\"baselineBeforeCurrentStory\":611,\"expectedAfterCurrentStory\":613,\"latestActualTotal\":613},\"commitReadiness\":{\"state\":\"not-ready\",\"reason\":\"Caller ruling is still required before impl-lead commit.\"},\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\"]},\"cleanupHandoff\":{\"acceptedRiskItems\":[],\"deferredItems\":[{\"description\":\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null}],\"cleanupRequired\":true},\"rulingRequest\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001-ruling-018\",\"decisionType\":\"project-scoped-refresh-semantics\",\"question\":\"For project-scoped source attachments shown in the project shell, what should refresh do when the attachment is stale or not_hydrated but there is no single unambiguous current process working-copy target?\",\"defaultRecommendation\":\"Hide or disable the project-shell refresh control unless the backend can identify exactly one current process working-copy target; keep refresh enabled for process-scoped rows and for project-scoped rows with one unambiguous owning process. This avoids falsely promising recovery and aligns with AC-3.2 until a later story defines cross-process/project-level hydration semantics.\",\"evidence\":[\"Verifier finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity is blocking and affects AC-3.2, AC-3.3, TC-3.2a, TC-3.2c, and TC-3.3a.\",\"Client project source section renders refresh controls for any stale or not_hydrated source regardless of scope.\",\"RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor returns SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source.\",\"All gates passed, but verifier outcome is needs-human-ruling because story-local requirements do not define project-scoped refresh target selection.\"],\"allowedResponses\":[\"Disable/hide project-shell refresh unless a single current process target exists; continue implementation to make UI truthful.\",\"Define project-scoped refresh to automatically select or create a runtime target; continue implementation with that behavior.\",\"Treat project-scoped refresh ambiguity as out of scope for Story 3 and allow current backend rejection despite the visible UI control.\",\"Block Story 3 until a separate design update defines project-scoped refresh semantics.\"]},\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"ask-ruling\"},\"startedFromPrimitiveArtifacts\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/001-story-validate.json\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"story-run-current\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-current.json\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-events\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-final-package\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-final-package.json\"},{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/002-story-orchestrate-run.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T19:34:03.502Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:10:05.331Z\"}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification/sonnet-review.md:169:| TC-4.2a | Given: Writable source with code work. When: Code checkpoint succeeds. Then: Durable code update in canonical source. | `tests/service/server/process-actions-api.test.ts:1217` \"TC-4.2a plans writable source code checkpoint targets\" | `checkpoint-planner.ts:16-31` includes `read_write` sources in `codeTargets`; `process-environment.service.ts:604-681` calls `codeCheckpointWriter.writeFor` for each code target | Planner test verifies code targets include writable sources. Integration test exercises full path. | **SATISFIED** |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification/sonnet-review.md:235:| TC-6.1a | Given: Prior env work + checkpoint. When: Reopen. Then: Latest durable state restored. | `tests/integration/process-work-surface.test.ts:312` \"TC-6.1a and TC-6.2a reopen keeps the Story 4 code checkpoint visible after the active environment is gone\"; `tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts:440` \"TC-6.1a bootstrap keeps the latest durable code checkpoint visible\" | `process-work-surface.service.ts:375-397` reads environment from durable store on every bootstrap | Integration test creates env with checkpoint, then reopens with absent environment -- checkpoint result still visible. Server test seeds absent env with prior checkpoint, verifies visibility. | **SATISFIED** |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification/gpt54-review.md:24:finding: Writable-source support does not compose from Story 2 into Story 4 on the real Convex path.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/epic-verification/gpt54-review.md:162:| TC-4.3a | SATISFIED | `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/checkpoint-planner.ts:16-24` | Read-only sources do not become code checkpoint targets. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
