ory 6 is the consumer of history-item visibility semantics.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/04-durable-checkpoint-of-artifacts-and-writable-sources/sonnet-review.md:126:1. No Story 4 TC directly requires that missing-source metadata be treated as read-only. The spec wording \"already-attached writable sources\" implies the normal case where sources are loaded.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/04-durable-checkpoint-of-artifacts-and-writable-sources/sonnet-review.md:157:2. **`process_event` history items not emitted at checkpoint settle.** Tech-design-server.md §processHistoryItems specifies writing `process_event` rows for \"latest checkpoint failed\" and \"checkpoint succeeded and changed canonical state.\" Story 4 has no explicit TC covering this, and the story DoD uses \"may\" not \"must.\" This is a design gap that Story 6 or a hardening item should close before live history browsing matters.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/03-controlled-execution-and-live-environment-state/sonnet-review.md:106:### Story 4 boundary — no canonical checkpoint writes\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/03-controlled-execution-and-live-environment-state/sonnet-review.md:135:**Validation step:** Story 4 implementer may add these at next opportunity or accept the existing partial coverage.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/03-controlled-execution-and-live-environment-state/sonnet-review.md:144:**Validation step:** Acceptable as-is given client layer covers the claim. Future Story 4 implementer may strengthen if desired.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/story-verification/04-durable-checkpoint-of-artifacts-and-writable-sources/green-phase-report.md