itory identity, source attachment summaries, source provenance entries, refresh responses, detach responses, and source-management error codes\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/00-foundation.md:204:- Fixtures cover exact duplicate, missing target ref duplicate, project/process scope coexistence, process-scoped shadowing, pending refresh, soft detach, unavailable source, and degraded provenance\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:25:- `lastHydratedAt` and `freshnessReason` visibility\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:41:- Story 2 source metadata visibility\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:5:Allow users to attach GitHub-backed repositories to a project or one process, with durable identity, scope visibility, duplicate protection, and invalid/inaccessible repository rejection.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process.md:29:- Immediate visibility of repository identity and scope after create\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:49:| 1 | What exact browser interaction model should attach, update, refresh, and detach use without creating a separate source-management app? | Extend the existing project shell and process work surface. Project-scoped actions appear in the project source section; process-scoped actions appear in the process materials/source area. Client calls Fastify JSON APIs and renders settled/pending/degraded responses in-place. No standalone source app or live source subscription is added. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:50:| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:95:| Processes | Core architecture | Process-scoped attachments, current-source views, and source provenance appear in the process work surface |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:99:| Archive | Core architecture | Downstream consumer only; Epic 6 provides source provenance that Epic 7 can reference |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:170:├── sourceProvenance.ts                          # NEW: durable source provenance records and process reads\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:174:├── schemas.ts                                   # MODIFIED: source summary fields, source provenance schemas\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:199:└── source-attachment-section.ts                 # MODIFIED: management controls and pending/degraded state display\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--so