/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:420:      - \"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:423:      - \"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:450:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:176-187` catches every non-`UNAUTHENTICATED` failure from `getProcessSourceProvenance` and returns `{ entries: [] }`. `apps/platform/client/features/processes/source-provenance-section.ts:37-42` renders any empty `entries` list as `No source provenance has been recorded for this process yet.` The current client tests only cover a true-empty response and degraded entry rendering (`tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts:11-45`); they do not cover this bootstrap failure path. In production, a 403/404/500 or transient provenance read failure is therefore presented as a real no-provenance process, which violates TC-4.1b's empty-state semantics and the story's anti-shim rule against fake runtime fallbacks.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:465:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:176-187` catches every non-`UNAUTHENTICATED` failure from `getProcessSourceProvenance` and returns `{ entries: [] }`. `apps/platform/client/features/processes/source-provenance-section.ts:37-42` renders any empty `entries` list as `No source provenance has been recorded for this process yet.` The current client tests only cover a true-empty response and degraded entry rendering (`tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts:11-45`); they do not cover this bootstrap failure path. In production, a 403/404/500 or transient provenance read failure is therefore presented as a real no-provenance process, which violates TC-4.1b's empty-state semantics and the story's anti-shim rule against fake runtime fallbacks.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:517:      path: \"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/004-verify.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:528:path: /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:544:      storyId: \"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:547:      id: \"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canoni