-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:466:        title: \"The required `redacted` provenance visibility branch is declared but never implemented\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:467:        evidence: \"Story 4 requires `currentAttachmentVisibility` to support `redacted` and explicitly says the service must redact current attachment details on access loss (`04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:123-143`). The shared enum still advertises `redacted` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts:58-63`, but `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:178-220` only emits `available`, `detached`, or `unavailable`. Repository search found no server or test implementation beyond the enum (`rg -n \\\"redacted\\\" apps convex tests` only matches the schema).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:502:        id: \"story4-redacted-visibility-unimplemented\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:504:        title: \"The required `redacted` provenance visibility branch is declared but never implemented\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:505:        evidence: \"Story 4 requires `currentAttachmentVisibility` to support `redacted` and explicitly says the service must redact current attachment details on access loss (`04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:123-143`). The shared enum still advertises `redacted` in `apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts:58-63`, but `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:178-220` only emits `available`, `detached`, or `unavailable`. Repository search found no server or test implementation beyond the enum (`rg -n \\\"redacted\\\" apps convex tests` only matches the schema).\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:535:        - \"AC-4.4 access-revocation `redacted` branch\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:551:      - \"The live provenance API cannot emit `currentAttachmentVisibility: redacted`; access-loss cases currently collapse into `unavailable` because `buildSourceProvenanceEntry()` has no redacted branch.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:567:      path: \"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/007-verify.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:578:path: /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:594:      storyId: \"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:597:      id: \"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:599:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 4 end-to-end by adding durable source provenance persistence and read APIs, recording informed-work and received-code-update provenance during execution/checkpoint flows, and rendering a process work-surface provenance section with Story 4 API/service/client coverage.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:609:        reason: \"Wired the new source provenance service into Fastify and the environment service.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:615:        reason: \"Extended store interfaces and implementations with durable source provenance create/list support.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:618:        reason: \"Added Convex mutation/query functions for persisting and listing source provenance rows.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:621:        reason: \"Added client API loading for process source provenance.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:627:        reason: \"Added source provenance to default client state.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:630:        reason: \"Extended process-surface state schema with source provenance.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:639:        reason: \"Added Story 4 API coverage for informing, receiving, and degraded provenance responses.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:645:        reason: \"Added Story 4 client coverage for empty and degraded provenance states.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:675:        - \"Covered the Story 4 read-only exclusion, degraded entry fallback, empty state, and API rendering paths with automated tests.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:691:      path: \"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:700:path: /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/004-verify.json\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:716:      storyId: \"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:719:      id: \"04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:723:      - \"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:726:      - \"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/003-implementor.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:753:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:176-187` catches every non-`UNAUTHENTICATED` failure from `getProcessSourceProvenance` and returns `{ entries: [] }`. `apps/platform/client/features/processes/source-provenance-section.ts:37-42` renders any empty `entries` list as `No source provenance has been recorded for this process yet.` The current client tests only cover a true-empty response and degraded entry rendering (`tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts:11-45`); they do not cover this bootstrap failure path. In production, a 403/404/500 or transient provenance read failure is therefore presented as a real no-provenance process, which violates TC-4.1b's empty-state semantics and the story's anti-shim rule against fake runtime fallbacks.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:768:        evidence: \"`apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:176-187` catches every non-`UNAUTHENTICATED` failure from `getProcessSourceProvenance` and returns `{ entries: [] }`. `apps/platform/client/features/processes/source-provenance-section.ts:37-42` renders any empty `entries` list as `No source provenance has been recorded for this process yet.` The current client tests only cover a true-empty response and degraded entry rendering (`tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts:11-45`); they do not cover this bootstrap failure path. In production, a 403/404/500 or transient provenance read failure is therefore presented as a real no-provenance process, which violates TC-4.1b's empty-state semantics and the story's anti-shim rule against fake runtime fallbacks.\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:820:      path: \"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/004-verify.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:865:Path: /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/story-lead/001-current.json\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-