{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated the Story 4 blockers in the existing change set without widening scope.\n\n[process-environment.service.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts) now records `received_code_update` provenance for the subset of writable checkpoint targets that actually succeeded, even if a sibling target later fails the overall checkpoint. I added a regression in [process-live-updates.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts) to prove that partial-success path.\n\n[source-provenance.service.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts) now honors the required redacted read path: degraded provenance with `access_revoked` returns `currentAttachmentVisibility: 'redacted'` and null current-attachment enrichment fields instead of leaking live attachment context. API coverage is in [source-management-api.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts). I also fixed the client regression in [process-response-composer.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/client/process-response-composer.test.ts) by restoring the jsdom test environment so `document`/`window` are available again.\n\nVerification passed:\n- `pnpm vitest run tests/service/client/process-response-composer.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts`\n- `pnpm run test:service`\n- `pnpm run test:client`"}}
